{
  "summary": "Pick a distinctive, implementable mission-control design for the Labmate cockpit",
  "agentCount": 4,
  "logs": [],
  "result": {
    "components": [
      {
        "region": "STATUS STRIP (persistent top, 40px, full-width, --surf-2, hairline bottom, grid area `strip`)",
        "notes": "Always-visible global readout. Left→right: study id `study_01HZX` in JetBrains Mono --text-muted; objective truncated (Archivo 13/18, ellipsis); target chip `breached_sla` and primary-metric chip `recall_at_fpr` (mono, --surf-3 pill, square 2px corners); live budget gauge rendering `trials 3/12 · 412s/900s` as two thin --cyan fill bars over --surf-3 track that advance while any run is `running`; far right a GLOBAL STATUS LAMP = color+glyph+label (`◉ RUNNING` cyan / `● IDLE` muted / `✕ FLAG` red). The lamp and an indeterminate --cyan top-of-viewport hairline (grafted from manuscript) animate whenever runs[].status includes `running`. On a leakage/test_set_tuning critique the lamp flips red and the strip prints `⚠ METHODOLOGICAL FLAG: LEAKAGE` (Orbitron, tracked) — read instantly from across a room. Empty study: lamp `● IDLE`, gauge shows `trials 0/— · 0s/—`."
      },
      {
        "region": "1. BRIEF + RUBRIC (left rail cols 1-3, top, grid area `brief`)",
        "notes": "Panel header: corner ticks + Orbitron `§01 BRIEF` (section number grafted from manuscript). Body: objective (Archivo 15/20), target + task_type, MetricSpec.primary with one-line rationale, Budget as `max_trials` / `budget_seconds` mono readouts, study.status chip (`open`/`done`/`stopped`). Derived guardrails render as mono chips from parsed feedback: `FPR ≤ 0.20`, `recall > precision`. 'Definition of done' = vertical LAMP CHECKLIST mapping the rubric required checks (○ pending / ◑ running amber / ● pass --st-completed / ✕ fail --st-failed), each row `glyph + label` in mono. `caught_an_issue` row is the one that flips ● green at the demo climax — give it slightly heavier weight. Empty/pre-grade: all lamps ○ dim with label `AWAITING`."
      },
      {
        "region": "2. DATA CONTRACT (left rail cols 1-3, below brief, grid area `contract`)",
        "notes": "Header `§02 DATA CONTRACT`. Top line: `row_count` in 28px Orbitron-adjacent mono + file_hash truncated mono. Then a RULED COLUMN TABLE (manuscript hairline rules between rows): column name (mono), dtype chip, missingness as a tiny inline % + 24px horizontal --cyan-dim bar. Leakage-flagged rows (dataset_version candidate leakage cols, default banned) get a --crit-leakage left border tint + a `[BAN]` ghost button (mono, amber outline). When a column is banned it shows a struck name + `BANNED` chip. Split strategy printed as a one-liner mono: `time(created_at) 70/15/15 · seed 42`. The Ban action is the click target in demo step 3. Empty: ruled skeleton rows + `NO CONTRACT — RUN profile_dataset` micro-label."
      },
      {
        "region": "3. EXPERIMENT CARDS (center cols 4-8, top, grid area `cards`)",
        "notes": "Header `§03 EXPERIMENT CARDS`. Stacked deck, one card per Hypothesis. Each card: falsifiable `statement` in Archivo 20/24 (the headline); `rationale` in Archivo 13/18 --text-sec; `model_family` chip + candidate `features[]` as small mono chips (banned/leaky features rendered struck); `expected_outcome` italic-toned line; latest linked run's primary metric in 40px JetBrains Mono tabular (the big readout, count-up tween on update, scramble-then-settle while running — grafted from phosphor); status chip top-right (proposed=amber / approved=cyan / rejected=muted struck). Footer: Approve / Deny / Rerun as a SEGMENTED CONTROL (mono labels, active = --cyan fill). When a test_set_tuning or leakage critique targets this card's run, the card gets the --alert-edge left bar + a `⚠ TEST-SET TUNING` mono banner in its margin. Empty: single dim corner-ticked ghost card `[ + PROPOSE HYPOTHESIS ]` (grafted from phosphor)."
      },
