13	        "fix": "Stabilize the callback reference passed to ToastItem. Option 1 - use useMemo at the call site (line 30):
```typescript
const removers = useMemo(() => new Map(toasts.map(t => [t.id, () => remove(t.id)])), [toasts, remove])
// Then in the map:
<ToastItem key={t.id} toast={t} onDone={removers.get(t.id)!} />
```

Option 2 (simpler) - pass the ID as a prop and stabilize the callback in ToastItem:
```typescript
// Line 30:
<ToastItem key={t.id} toast={t} toastId={t.id} onDone={remove} />

// ToastItem signature and effect:
function ToastItem({ toast, toastId, onDone }: { toast: Toast; toastId: number; onDone: (id: number) => void }) {
  useEffect(() => {
    const timer = window.setTimeout(() => onDone(toastId), 4200)
    return () => window.clearTimeout(timer)
  }, [onDone, toastId])
```

The second option is clearer: it passes the stable `remove` function directly, and the ID as a separate prop, making dependencies explicit."
